(449, '-xö£a#1', '-xötla', 'xotla', 'xO£A', 'cut lengthwise', 'cortar a la larga', 'Evidence for the length of the vowels comes from the following modern\r\ndialects:\r\nCoatepec C. and Zacapoaxtla where the word means ´apuntar´ (i.e. make lines),\r\nfrom Pipil where it means ´to wound´, and from La Huasteca where it means ´to\r\nroot up´.\r\n'),
