(33, '-të¹=£a-kos=aw=ki', '-tëuctla-cozauhqui', 'teuctlacoçauhqui', 'tE¹£AkOsAwkI', '\"snake\"', '\"culebra\"', 'Our analysis of this word is based on CF11.78v: Auh injc mjtoa\r\ntecutlacoçauhquj: itech qujça in tecutli, yoan coçauhquj: injc mjtoa\r\ntecutlacoçauhquj, qujl imachcauh in cocoa; yoan injc mjtoa tecutli \r\nAnd therefore it is called tecutlacoçauhqui: it comes from tecutli ´lord´ and\r\ncoçauhqui ´yellow´, they say it is the lord of the snakes; and it is called\r\ntecutli ´lord´.\r\nThe morpheme tla is the archaic form of the absolutive suffix tli.\r\n', 4, 4, 0, NULL, '\r\n'),
