(42, '-tök=tia', '-töctia', 'toctia', 'tOktIA', 'hide', 'esconder', 'F.Karttunen considers this word, meaning ´hide´, to be derived from toka\r\n´follow´ and therefore assigns it a short vowel, o, she supports the\r\nhypothesis with Tetelcingo toktia ´se acompaña con el´ and with Zacapoaxtla\r\ntoktia ´se encarga´. J. Campbell assumes it to be derived from töka ´bury´.\r\nWe agree with J. Campbell in seeing a connection between ´bury´ and ´hide´.\r\n', 12, 2, 1, NULL, '=ti+´\r\n'),
