(755, '-²äwa', '-tzähua', 'tzahua', '²AwA', 'spin thread', 'hilar', 'Tzähua seems to have been intransitive in the sixteenth century: Molina\r\ngives it as an intransitive; in Sahagún someone who spins is tzäuhqui, what\r\nis spun tzähualli, and the act of spinning is in Molina tzähualiztli.\r\nIn some modern dialects the verb is transitive, Zacapoaxtla, Mecayapan,\r\nCoatepec, etc.; in some it is intransitive, Pipil, Huazalinguillo, etc.; and\r\nin Tetelcingo it is used both transitively and intransitively.\r\n', 10, 8, 1, NULL, '-²äw\r\n'),
