(129, '-£aöko=lia', '-tlaöcolia', 'tlaocolia', '£AOkOlIA', 'take pity on', 'tener piedad de', 'According to Molina tlaocolia takes one object; this is confirmed by the\r\nexample from CF11, fol. 8.34-35, ac ye in nictlaocoliz ´who is the one I\r\nshall take pity on?´ The meaning of the word in this sentence also\r\ncorresponds to Molina´s gloss \"hazer misericordia a otro\".\r\nHowever, in Codex Aubin it systematically occurs with two objects and with\r\na slightly different meaning, ´give out of pity´. This is true also of the\r\none example of the reverential form tlaocolilia. The word tlaocoltia is in\r\nCodex Aubin constructed with one object and appears to mean ´take pity on´.\r\n', 11, 2, 1, NULL, '=li+´\r\n'),
(661, '-£aöko=li=lia', '-tlaöcolilia', 'tlaocolilia', '£AOkOlIlIA', 'take pity on', 'tener piedad de', 'See the comment to the verb tlaocolia.\r\n', 12, 2, 1, NULL, '=li+´\r\n'),
