(208, '-£AxIlA-kal+li', '-tlAxIlA-calli', 'tlaxilacalli', '£AxIlAkAl', 'quarter', 'barrio', 'FKarttunen writes this word tlahxillacal-li (-tla´xilla-kal+li) and bases the\r\nglottal stop on one attestation in a testament from Culhuacan, 1577; a glotal\r\nstop in that position suggests the root -a´zi, maybe =tla-/a/´xi=l=tla´-kal+li;\r\nbut this analysis is not an obvious one, and there is variation between single\r\nl and double l in the sources. The double l is found in Clavijero (18th century\r\n1974) and in various land documents; the entry in Molina has single l.\r\nWe leave the word partly unanalyzed and the three vowels unmarked for length\r\nand glottal stop hoping that some one will stumble upon convincing evidence for\r\nan anlysis of this word.\r\n', 0, 0, 0, NULL, '\r\n'),
