(1742, 6, 1, 15, '', '', '', '-ka -wel +t-äxkä+w +to=£a-tki -in -£äl+²in£i -in +t-öme-x+tin -in -teö=yö=ti-ka +no-nämik < Isabel >', 'Ca huel tascauh. totlatqui.  y~ tlaltzintli y~ tomestin y~ teoyotica nonamic. Isabel', 'The land REV is truely the property, the belonging of both of us, [and] my legitimate wife, Isabel.'),
(1743, 6, 1, 16, '', '', '', '-aw -in -äxkän +to-yö(n)l=lO=ko=pa +tikto-maki=lia+´ -in +to-£aso´-ta´+²in < padre fray Francisco de Loaysa vicario. > -in +ï-pan < santa iglesia villa de > -koyö=wa´-kän', 'auh yn asca~ toyon llocopa tictomaquilia yn totlaçotatzin padre fray franco* de loaysa Vic .  yn ipa~ santa yglesia Villa de coyohuacan', 'And now voluntarily we give REV it to our beloved father REV, padre fray Franco de Loaysa, vicar in the holy church of the town of Coyohuacan.'),
